You aren't making a fair comparison.

In tournament play (i.e. devnull) it would be possible for someone (or
a group of people, working together) to pull off Shawn's stunt without
breaking any of the already established tournament rules.

The game of chess has a precisely defined and formalized set of
rules.  These rules govern everything from player behavior, time, the
size of the pieces, the size of the playing board, &c.  Even minutiae
is covered.  In order to adjust a playing piece on the board, a player
must first inform his opponent of his intent.  A player who fails to
do so is required, by rule, to move the first piece he touches.

I believe the behavior you described would be deemed cheating by the
rules of chess.

